WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.422
(baby birds chirping)

00:00:01.422 --> 00:00:05.260
(gentle string music)

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.723
- I am attracted to the bluebirds
because of their beauty.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.363
My name is Al Larson.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.703
I am 97 years old-or young.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.230
These bluebirds are about 11 days old.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:27.323
I've helped over 40,000 nestlings.

00:00:27.323 --> 00:00:29.050
(string music)

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.253
Every living thing has just
as much right to live as I do.

00:00:38.568 --> 00:00:41.318
(birds chirping)

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.010
I'm a birdwatcher by choice, I guess.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.253
When I retired in the late '70s,

00:00:50.253 --> 00:00:53.790
that's 1970's, I came upon this article

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:57.315
in National Geographic
and I became aware of

00:00:57.315 --> 00:01:00.540
the plight of the
bluebird. Their population

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.289
has been declining, and
the importance of the

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:06.920
nest box to the survival of
the bluebirds, and I thought,

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.470
well, why don't I try that here?

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.110
So one of the first nest boxes I set up

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:18.110
a bluebird moved into it and
immediately, hey, success.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.833
I should put up more boxes.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.500
Oh, this is a second nest.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.960
You can see different
material built on top there.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.953
Well, I'll go on to the next box now.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.770
See what's going on there.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.030
(flowing piano music)

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:40.030
These nest boxes that I use
are ones that I built at home.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:42.660
I came up with a solution of

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.160
building the box as simply as possible.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.580
Cheap to build, with just four
sides, a bottom, and a roof.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.170
Anybody could build it, even kids.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.170
Over the years I have added
more than 350 nest boxes out.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:03.580
My bluebird trails cover quite
an area in southwest Idaho.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.410
Actually, I've got a trail

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:07.163
in each of five different counties.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.430
I monitor the boxes
regularly to record the data

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.970
of what goes on with the development

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.050
of the nesting cycle of the bluebirds.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:22.090
I've shared my data with
Boise State University,

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.440
the Banding Laboratory
at Patuxent, Maryland,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.193
and anybody else who requested.

00:02:29.964 --> 00:02:31.864
♪ Pretty little bluebird ♪

00:02:31.864 --> 00:02:34.041
♪ where do you go ♪

00:02:34.041 --> 00:02:37.103
♪ Come back, come back to me ♪

00:02:37.103 --> 00:02:41.456
♪ I'm going says the
bird as he flew on high ♪

00:02:41.456 --> 00:02:45.873
♪ To see if my color matches the sky ♪

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.520
I'm gratified to know

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.670
that I've helped the bluebirds
increase their population.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.360
I'm gratified to know that
through the work I've done

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.470
I've inspired many, many
other people to help

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:03.523
not only bluebirds, but
other creatures as well.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.653
So maybe I've been put here
to help our environment.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.780
My message is, you've got to be active

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.600
if you're going to get old.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.500
Don't crawl into a cocoon

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.400
because you might not break out of it.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:25.440
So think about the future,
and what you can do tomorrow.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.593
Plan ahead.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.685
(birds chirping)

00:03:32.685 --> 00:03:35.268
(musical tone)

